{"id": "59378eca-92fc-4f72-80ce-8d54ed38b6b2", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I should also note ModelSetupTime reflects cold-start launch time for serverless compute resources, and touch on how provisioned concurrency affects billing.

The pattern here — 9s p99 only on first idle requests, nothing during busy hours — points clearly to idle-triggered cold starts rather than scaling-driven ones, so a small provisioned concurrency setting (1-2, within MaxConcurrency of 5) should cover it, though bursts above that threshold would still cold start. Alternatives worth weighing include keep-warm pings, scheduled autoscaling of provisioned concurrency for business hours, shrinking the model/container, or switching to a real-time endpoint if latency sensitivity is constant — the right call depends on SLA tolerance and how consistent the traffic pattern is, and I should flag that the p99 figures are likely based on very few datapoints during idle periods.

